1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:08,633
Visitors to Daejeon crowd into one famous bakery, and rarely go on to the next stop.

2
00:00:09,067 --> 00:00:16,600
Daejeon Detour is a web app you open from a QR code. First, pick your language.

3
00:00:17,033 --> 00:00:23,600
The Old Downtown half-day course links four stops on foot.

4
00:00:24,033 --> 00:00:33,000
Check the store info and the not-affiliated notice, then tap plus to add items.

5
00:00:33,433 --> 00:00:38,700
Your items turn into a Korean order sentence, with a reading guide.

6
00:00:39,133 --> 00:00:49,100
Say it back, and see the recognition match. It is not a pronunciation grade.

7
00:00:49,533 --> 00:00:57,500
Stuck? Show the screen. Staff reply with one tap, shown in your language.

8
00:00:57,933 --> 00:01:08,300
Next stop, Gwangcheon Sikdang. It is dine-in only, so the to-go line is left out.

9
00:01:08,733 --> 00:01:20,000
For the city, an operator report shows where visitors went after the bakery. The numbers are sample data.

10
00:01:20,433 --> 00:01:28,767
Daejeon Detour. After the bakery, one more stop.
